<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Karl I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1916">1916</a>–<a href="/years/1918">1918</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Charles I of Austria</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Karl I, or Charles I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>, was the last Emperor of Austria and King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>, reigning from 1916 to 1918. He sought a separate peace during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a> without success. With defeat in 1918 he withdrew from state affairs as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austro-Hungarian Empire</a> dissolved.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/karl-i.jpg" alt="Karl I" width="293" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hermann Clemens Kosel · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Karl_I.,_Kaiser_von_%C3%96sterreich_(1887-1922).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
